      "description": "Real-time model of a Soviet L-1U1 diamond pantograph (current collector of an electric train), rebuilt from an engineering CAD assembly for XR, simulation and synthetic data generation.\n\nThe animation shows an example of maintenance procedure. The pantograph lowers, the clamps open, a worn contact strip is replaced with a new one, and the pantograph rises back to working height.\n\n- 30,648 triangles (from 2.35M in the original CAD)\n- 3 texture sets at 2K, PBR metal/roughness\n- 18 joint rig with 2-bone IK and a raise control\n- Morph targets showing wear of each strip, used to generate a labelled synthetic dataset for computer vision\n\nModelled and rigged in Maya, baked in Marmoset Toolbag, textured in Substance 3D Painter.\n\nBased on the CAD model \"Pantograph L-1U1-01\" by Igor Lavrukhin (GrabCAD)."
